iotes and they  don't like stones at all  brock then considers whether they should  pay this spider-man a visit in new york  the mid-credits scenes and spider-man on  their way home is linked to the  mid-credits scenes in venom let there be  carnage after seeing spider-man on the  way home his teleportation into the mcu  makes a little bit more sense and it's  all because of that strange spell though  it's unclear as to why bronx is there in  the first place after all he's never met  us peter parker it's not something we've  ever heard in any of the venom films he  doesn't even know a spider-man in his  universe let alone a guy named peter  parker this seems to be one massive plot  hole if you haven't seen the mid credit  scenes of what is venom that thereby  carnage  perhaps venom knows as he claims to have  80 billion light years of hive knowledge  spanning the multiverse in venom to  credit scenes it stands to reason that  his hive knowledge would contain  information about peter parker's status  as spider-man so perhaps venom was drawn  in by the spell and eddie was forced to  accompany him it is also maybe because  venom was about to share a tiny bit of  the hive knowledge with eddie when they  were automatically teleported into the  mcu as the multiverse also included toby  maguire's spider-man  and let me remind you that this  spider-man has fought a version of venom  before in his universe and it knew peter  parker was spider-man so it stands to  reason that the shared hive mind would  have that knowledge in it  so anyway the bartender wants brock to  settle the bill before he leaves for new  york to look for spider-man but at the  same time all venom wants to do a skinny  dip which isn't such a bad idea after a  few tequilas believe me  but before any of that can happen  strange's second spell from the end of  spider-man the way home kicks in sending  brock back to his universe but there is  one black smudge that was left behind in  this event and it starts